<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UK police arrest dual UK-Iranian national over Fairford air base incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae51894d2d319b5d8a33e3c91b495e32bab3a5b6af8f682cbbf2aead11444fd4</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T19:40:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident--eddc8f085ba4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident" /><summary type="html">British police on Thursday arrested a British-Iranian dual national in connection with the security incident at the Fairford airbase Wednesday. Five other men initially arrested over the incidence were later released without charge on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France’s purchasing power crisis: Navigating the pinch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2814896ca5094f4815e7c038b131cb66c1c4cbff3437b53e79a3284ab689edb</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T19:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/economy/20261001-france-s-purchasing-power-crisis-navigating-the-pinch--b9a1f8c10741.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/economy/20261001-france-s-purchasing-power-crisis-navigating-the-pinch" /><summary type="html">With looming elections and a draft budget that aims to address a €305.7bn financing requirement, French households are increasingly in the red. Will wages ever manage to outpace energy inflation?</summary><category term="Economy" /></entry><entry><title>'Guilty of all charges': Man City at centre of 'biggest scandal in football history', vows to appeal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8f798fe0ba8ea72190c16dd57093a6b344e0c4a67ad058e5f2be5212ebe11d6</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T16:37:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261001-guilty-of-all-charges-man-city-at-centre-of-biggest-scandal-in-football-history-vows-to-app--8c015176048c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261001-guilty-of-all-charges-man-city-at-centre-of-biggest-scandal-in-football-history-vows-to-appeal" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome our sports editor, James Vasina, and Andreas Evargora, sports journalist and commentator. Evargora describes the current Manchester City case as unprecedented in scale: “This is nothing of the scale that we’ve seen before.” The case brings together an explosive mix of pressures confronting modern sport like never before: the multibillion-euro business of football, the legal and regulatory mechanisms designed to govern it, and the increasingly complex relationship between sport, political power and international investment.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Students face riot police as protests over school conditions escalate in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d3d8e63ce19584b8b9ffd8019581fb2fe4e02b71c664d5c5683e0b8a9c997cc</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T15:42:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/students-face-riot-police-as-protests-over-school-conditions-escalate-in-france--2f89252a49c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/students-face-riot-police-as-protests-over-school-conditions-escalate-in-france" /><summary type="html">French teenagers on Tuesday set fire to rubbish bins and threw projectiles at police who responded with batons and tear gas, as pupils kept up blockades and protests at hundreds of high schools, demanding better conditions. The movement in the lycees, attended by students aged 15 to 18 for their final three years of secondary education in France, has angered the government.</summary></entry><entry><title>Teens block high schools across France, demand better conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e597e1bbd6514b06ac3ba69768d36ea36e9b7cd47f5ec35ca4c045f8eee4ed</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T15:25:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-teens-block-high-schools-across-france-demand-better-conditions--656527cb1b55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-teens-block-high-schools-across-france-demand-better-conditions" /><summary type="html">France's prime minister convened a crisis meeting on Thursday and canceled ministers' trips to focus on the nationwide spread of protests, some violent, by high school students venting against under-resourced schools, long hours and other complaints. The demonstrations erupted in Paris-region schools last week and have snowballed, with police making hundreds of arrests in clashes with the young protesters. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rethinking traditional designs: A French twist on the kimono</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50865bac2438ee4890da9d7abae191fb18f021772d2b6c942cf43eb2551a7505</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T15:16:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261001-rethinking-traditional-designs-a-french-twist-on-the-kimono--bf613d3951e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261001-rethinking-traditional-designs-a-french-twist-on-the-kimono" /><summary type="html">In this episode of Entre Nous, Delano D'Souza welcomes Alice Kith, a Paris-based designer reimagining the traditional kimono through a contemporary French lens. Her brand A-Kith brings together heritage, craftsmanship and modern Parisian style. From Poiret to Kenzo, we explore influences and how the kimono is woven into the history of Parisian fashion.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Cameroon govt announces payments as teachers strike continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa795b72ae90f9a0b41bbb246d235c3b5415fc31eff35f901a7239296485b683</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-cameroon-govt-announces-payments-as-teachers-strike-continues--2797b31873b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-cameroon-govt-announces-payments-as-teachers-strike-continues" /><summary type="html">In Cameroon, the start of the academic year for Universities, scheduled for October 5, may not take place. This is as a result of an indefinite strike launched by SYNES, the National Union of Higher Education Teachers. Teachers are demanding the payment of 16 billion CFA francs in academic bonuses, equivalent to nearly 24 million euros.</summary></entry><entry><title>A blessing or a curse? New Caledonia's dwindling nickel industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d55006b9f19f21e93da4456adc9ba856b2a81f6404b86a9ae185e280e9a8dc</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:07:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry--cc6e1bce2bc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry" /><summary type="html">This Thursday October 1, the French government is holding a summit aimed at attracting investors and revitalising wealth creation in France's overseas territories. Among the assets Paris wants to highlight is New Caledonian nickel. But the industry has been severely weakened by the political deadlock and tensions that have rocked the archipelago in recent years.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Sheer devastation: '80 percent of Gazan infrastructure has been destroyed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01981196183fafb08cf61fdfeb6ffa1783b56a1e8a626c15149759748010ad0d</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed--aa956df4e191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed" /><summary type="html">New images posted this week by Google Maps show the utter destruction in Gaza. It's been estimated that 61 tonnes of rubble need to be cleared – that's 20 times the amount of rubble generated in all wars across the world over the last 18 years.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>From Billie Eilish to Cardi B: Hassan Hajjaj on the stars who stepped into his colourful world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e845ec3dba84abb92125bc74aea806be713ba2ac134d7a5255fc9ae86af49058</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:06:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261001-from-billie-eilish-to-cardi-b-hassan-hajjaj-on-the-stars-who-stepped-into-his-colourful-wor--1edbf8b97dd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261001-from-billie-eilish-to-cardi-b-hassan-hajjaj-on-the-stars-who-stepped-into-his-colourful-world" /><summary type="html">Moroccan-British artist and photographer Hassan Hajjaj has photographed some of the biggest names in music and pop culture – from Madonna, Billie Eilish and Alicia Keys to Cardi B and Lee "Scratch" Perry. Now, 40 of his vibrant "Rock Stars" are on show at Paris's Philharmonie. Hajjaj tells us how he creates his instantly recognisable portraits, blends Moroccan heritage with London street culture – and what happens when a global superstar steps in front of his camera.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Behind the scenes of Céline Dion's high-tech gig - Tech 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4103c450c561fbbbed3b21d62c41ef4db5e96baf03fc089929a1dfc2543e8d2</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:03:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-behind-the-scenes-of-c_line-dion-s-high-tech-gig-tech-24--d0c3104b48fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-behind-the-scenes-of-c%C3%A9line-dion-s-high-tech-gig-tech-24" /><summary type="html">🎤 #CélineDion is making her great comeback with a 16-day residency in #France after years of illness. To keep her stage quiet and her voice crisp, her team is using both AI and high-tech sound systems.
 
#FRANCE24's Peter O'Brien went behind the scenes at the invitation of French audio company L-Acoustics ☝️</summary></entry><entry><title>UK, France end 'on in, one out' Channel migrant exchange deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228fdc168cefd49d394bc3667d223882abc55c5c97a6dc9cefa6b0613edc9560</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:44:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-uk-france-end-on-in-one-out-channel-migrant-exchange-deal--d86e46b7757d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-uk-france-end-on-in-one-out-channel-migrant-exchange-deal" /><summary type="html">A year-old deal between France and Britain to return migrants crossing the Channel illegally on small boats has come to an end, the UK interior ministry said Wednesday. The deal was agreed under former UK prime minister Keir Starmer last year in a bid to help a post-Brexit reset by easing what had become a major source of tension between the neighbours.</summary></entry><entry><title>France demands belt-tightening in 2027 budget as investors sour on its debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8196ff28da9d252b7da896cdfa6e36302b9c2998ffbf711b6ff1a6eb0a01b9c3</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:42:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-demands-belt-tightening-in-2027-budget-as-investors-sour-on-its-debt--bf1952c0ff96.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-demands-belt-tightening-in-2027-budget-as-investors-sour-on-its-debt" /><summary type="html">France presented its ​2027 budget bill on Thursday, seeking to enact unpopular belt-tightening measures that can lower its deficit and appease increasingly twitchy bond investors ahead of next year's presidential election. The legislation faces a tough ride in a deeply divided parliament, as political clans position themselves for one of the country's most consequential elections in modern times.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s 2027 budget plan puts pressure on local services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb370f916a17abcc7646ce77b7986ac5340c8a08cf1f5f921299bf4b65d4c6e6</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:42:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-s-2027-budget-plan-puts-pressure-on-local-services--135b555a9d97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-s-2027-budget-plan-puts-pressure-on-local-services" /><summary type="html">France presented its ​2027 budget bill on Thursday, seeking to enact unpopular belt-tightening measures. And local governments are bracing for painful cuts. The national government provides most of the financing for local and municipal budgets – and it's now seeking 5.4 billion euros in savings there. Across the country, mayors are scrambling to figure out how to cut back, while still providing essential services.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pink October: Raising awareness about breast cancer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4c9049e40f068808fb1077d121324e2a97479b9e442c4939a9735eb585abe79</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-pink-october-raising-awareness-about-breast-cancer--025f898bc79c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-pink-october-raising-awareness-about-breast-cancer" /><summary type="html">Breast cancer is the leading cause of cancer-related deaths among women and more than 61,000 cases are diagnosed in France each year. At Paris's Curie Institute, researchers are trying to develop new ways to identify and treat different types of cancers. One trial involves developing so-called “tumors on a chip”: miniature models which are capable of recreating the characteristics of a tumor in vitro outside of their normal biological context.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know about the terrifying FlyDubai flight bound for Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:157b40d9e37ccddcf609c8d4bc3db4d6cffa868c6897c16e048db0f61d6d8f9f</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:38:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-what-to-know-about-the-terrifying-flydubai-flight-bound-for-israel--7c47d89b8afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-what-to-know-about-the-terrifying-flydubai-flight-bound-for-israel" /><summary type="html">A copilot stabbed a captain in an apparent attempt to crash a jetliner as it was flying 174 people to Israel on Wednesday. But passengers burst into the cockpit and wrestled with the attacker even as the plane descended sharply, witnesses and Israel’s government said. The plane made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia. The shaken passengers from the FlyDubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv landed Wednesday evening in Israel on another flight, as onlookers cheered.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gender-based violence: French proposed bill aims to strengthen protections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44c521371103b932cdb5e7f2d6960c9f0730a3c0498f203534ab418f509205f6</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:37:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-gender-based-violence-french-proposed-bill-aims-to-strengthen-protections--c3f0f7be8071.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-gender-based-violence-french-proposed-bill-aims-to-strengthen-protections" /><summary type="html">French lawmakers are set to debate a bill against gender-based and sexual violence. It aims to strengthen the entire process – from reporting crimes and investigation to protection and compensation for victims. The bill also targets online sexual abuse, including non-consensual content and AI-generated deepfakes. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds held, dozens wounded as French school protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c8fe7888a59af2a554963712df2fb5d7a3f907c5d2fa1e6395436e3f71cd81a</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-hundreds-held-dozens-wounded-as-french-school-protests-escalate--45e1b9ff1740.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-hundreds-held-dozens-wounded-as-french-school-protests-escalate" /><summary type="html">French security forces on Wednesday detained over 600 people while dozens of police and gendarmes were wounded as protests that have seen blockades of high schools and violent clashes escalated, the interior minister said. Since last week, students have staged protests outside schools over grievances ranging from timetables, class sizes and a shortage of teachers to overheated classrooms during this year's heatwaves. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum reports from Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>The hunting lobby: Behind France's rural power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7d607bb1eeaf3e7435abb5d57986ec264cfff1bd7e2eba80628566c91ea04ae</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:24:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261001-the-hunting-lobby-behind-france-s-rural-power--b264d6aacff2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261001-the-hunting-lobby-behind-france-s-rural-power" /><summary type="html">After football and fishing, France's third-favourite pastime is hunting. The ancestral activity is popular but also divisive, with passions running high between those who defend hunting traditions and a growing number of animal rights activists. Though it's become statistically safer, a majority of French people say they don’t feel secure walking in nature during hunting season. So what steps has the government taken to regulate hunting? And why is the hunting lobby so strong and influential? We take a closer look in this edition of French Connections.</summary><category term="French connections" /></entry><entry><title>US continues to be 'a very significant partner', UN peacekeeping chief says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fbd3228de34cf57c39f99f424dccc68250d8ab495177e8c3b8c779ff7e5edc6</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:14:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief--b044ef9ba027.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN peacekeeping chief Jean-Pierre Lacroix said the US continues to be "a very significant partner", despite owing $3 billion to peacekeeping. With the UN forced to cut about 25 percent of its capacity, Lacroix defended missions that cost just 0.2 percent of global military spending: "Peacekeeping is a good deal really."</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee death row inmate Christa Pike survives two lethal injections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9e749bef94c0f28da434f5df5a9e030ca7900c402534b531568de311b3e70a2</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:41:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-tennessee-death-row-inmate-christa-pike-survives-two-lethal-injections--e5f556068c44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-tennessee-death-row-inmate-christa-pike-survives-two-lethal-injections" /><summary type="html">A Tennessee woman convicted of a murder three decades ago survived two lethal injection doses on Wednesday, marking the state's second failed execution this year. Christa Pike, 50, had been set to become the first woman to be executed in the southern US state in 200 years. The botched execution prompted the state’s governor to halt the one remaining execution for the rest of the year and launch a “comprehensive review”.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are French students blocking their school entrances?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4736b558b1126afe1da9182cded9528e1a57b624a83d95f8ef20245d79508d0e</id><updated>2026-10-01T21:08:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-why-are-french-students-blocking-their-school-entrances--cb15e64a6f5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-why-are-french-students-blocking-their-school-entrances" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 🎒 🪧 High schoolers across #France continued to blockade their #schools on Thursday, trying to form a "blocus" at the entrances of their schools in #protest.
 
